Switch to a loaded game's scene before running the old scene's scripts.

Loading a game sets _tempTextBuffer to the saved scene's name and
switches to it on the next frame. Meanwhile, the current scene's
scripts ran once more and could start a dialogue, which writes its
answer id to the same buffer. After the raft's game over in the FLY
scenes, pressing L started OVER.DLG again, whose answer "1" was then
loaded as a scene: "ERROR: Unable to open '1'!". Skip the rest of
the frame after a load, so that nothing runs before the switch.

--- a/game.cpp
+++ b/game.cpp
@@ -280,6 +280,12 @@
 			_workaroundRaftFlySceneBug = strncmp(_currentSceneScn, "FLY", 3) == 0;
 		}
 		updateKeysPressedTable();
+		if (_switchScene) {
+			// A game was just loaded: switch to its scene on the next frame
+			// without running this scene's scripts, which could start a
+			// dialogue that overwrites the scene name in _tempTextBuffer.
+			break;
+		}
 		updateMouseButtonsPressed();
 		runObjectsScript();
 		if (_startDialogue) {
